<title>GERMANY: EMI chief - EU budgets situation clearer in summer.</title>
<headline>EMI chief - EU budgets situation clearer in summer.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Monetary Institute (EMI) President Alexandre Lamfalussy said on Tuesday that it should be possible to have an &quot;educated guess&quot; on the state of 1997 European national budgets by summer this year.</p>
<p>Lamfalussy, speaking at a news conference to mark the launch of the EMI's third annual report, said that by then second quarter economic data from, most of the countries planning to take part in monetary union should be available.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
